  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Siva Sankar vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 25 August, 2020 Author: D.Ramesh Bench: D.Ramesh The Honourable Sri Justice D.Ramesh Criminal Petition No.3362 of 2020 Order:",
    "facts": "This Criminal Petition is filed under Section 482 of Cr.P.C seeking quash of FIR in Cr.No.49 of 2020 of Pedakakani Police Station, Guntur Urban, Guntur District, registered against the petitioners for the offences punishable under Sections 353, 420, 272 & 273 IPC and Sections 57 & 58 r/w 36 and 30 of the Food Safety & Standards Act, 2006 (for short, 'the FSS Act') Heard learned counsel for the petitioners and the learned Additional Public Prosecutor.",
    "arguments": "When these matters are taken up for hearing, the learned counsel for the petitioners and the learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that this matter is squarely covered by earlier decisions of this Court, whereunder the accused against whom similar cases were registered on the basis of similar set of facts were [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court as the prosecution is not maintainable against them under law and also on the ground that Tobacco products would not fall within the definition of 'food' as defined under Section 3(i)(j) of FSS Act and that the police are not authorized to register the crime and investigate the same and to file the charge sheet. Therefore, learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that the petitioners herein also who are facing the prosecution on the same set of facts under the same sections of law are similarly placed and they are also entitled for quash of the proceedings.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "When these matters are taken up for hearing, the learned counsel for the petitioners and the learned Additional Public Prosecutor would submit that this matter is squarely covered by earlier decisions of this Court, whereunder the accused against whom similar cases were registered on the basis of similar set of facts were [LEAKAGE_MASK] by this Court as the prosecution is not maintainable against them under law and also on the ground that Tobacco products would not fall within the definition of 'food' as defined under Section 3(i)(j) of FSS Act and that the police are not authorized to register the crime and investigate the same and to file the charge sheet. Therefore, learned counsel for the petitioners would submit that the petitioners herein also who are facing the prosecution on the same set of facts under the same sections of law are similarly placed and they are also entitled for quash of the proceedings.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
